1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:03,890
A useful computer setup begins with the
task you want

2
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:07,450
to do. Suppose the words on a webpage are
hard

3
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:11,990
to read. Decide which control affects that
page, make one

4
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:15,970
change, and check the result before
changing anything else.

5
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:22,290
Browser zoom makes a webpage larger or
smaller. Display scaling

6
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:26,330
affects the wider desktop. If only the
webpage is difficult

7
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:30,730
to read, try browser zoom first. Use the
text size

8
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:35,630
controls when they are available, and
check that buttons and instructions remain
usable.

9
00:00:37,611 --> 00:00:41,671
When sound is missing, first check the
selected output device

10
00:00:41,671 --> 00:00:45,651
and mute setting. A connected headset may
be receiving the

11
00:00:45,651 --> 00:00:50,291
sound. Adjust the volume, then play a
short test. The

12
00:00:50,291 --> 00:00:55,251
same habit applies to printing: choose the
printer and inspect a test page.

13
00:00:57,264 --> 00:01:00,784
A practice calendar entry needs a title, a
start and

14
00:01:00,784 --> 00:01:05,144
end, a location, and a useful reminder. If
a partner

15
00:01:05,144 --> 00:01:09,484
only needs your availability, look for
free or busy sharing.

16
00:01:10,004 --> 00:01:14,824
Check the actual options instead of
assuming every service shares the same
details.

17
00:01:16,926 --> 00:01:20,326
Pause here and make one helpful adjustment
on your workstation.

18
00:01:20,926 --> 00:01:24,046
Show a partner what changed and explain
how to undo

19
00:01:24,046 --> 00:01:28,526
it. Before leaving a shared computer,
restore the lab settings

20
00:01:28,526 --> 00:01:32,446
and save your practice work. You now have
a repeatable

21
00:01:32,446 --> 00:01:35,486
routine: choose, test, and explain.
